>youngest could have been born yesterday.  

>. . . apart from giving them some genetic information, I have absolutely
>*nothing* to do with the raising of my kids.  

> . . . I note that Cognitex has RNA & DNA in it.  I guess I gave my kids
>some of that!

Am I insanely promiscuous, or just insane?  Neither--I was a sperm donor! 
So, you see, I probably have kids, but know virtually nothing about them.  

Some folks may think this still qualifies me as insane, but sperm donorship
was for me a very sensible activity.  I have very helpful genetic traits,
and am more than happy to share them with others.  By donating sperm, I am
assured of having lots of kids (a privilege that men have fought and died
for in times past), who will be raised by very devoted parents (you really
have to want to be a parent to go through artificial insemination), to the
mutual benefit of all parties involved (I get to spread my genes and earn
some bucks; the parents get strong, smart kids; my kids get an inborn edge
in the struggle to survive and thrive).  

I'm not averse to having kids through the usual means, but I certainly not
going to restrict my procreation to "natural" methods.  Think of it as
transhuman reproduction!


