It strikes me that Buddhism, Christianity, Islam, Protestantism are all
macromutants; suggesting that macromutation is less likely to be lethal in
memes than in genes.

The controversies that divided the early Christian church look (from the
outside) like micromutations; but for the most part, micromutations are
reabsorbed and forgotten, perhaps by the hygiene mentioned in "Snow Crash".
I guess that's why we don't see many pairs of sects in which cumulative
micromutation added up to divergence comparable to a macromutation; the only
example (in a formal religion) that occurs to me is the various branches of
Buddhism.

A macromutation in a meme-complex often creates a mating barrier, preventing
traffic of minor memes between the two populations.

