I sure hope Tom's "burdon of proof" doesn't mean we should *challenge* 
people to defend their non-extropian views on the list!  Not only would
that be putting them in a double bind, rules wise, but I usually don't 
want to hear the arguments!  Tom suggests asking for references, which 
sounds nice and quiet, but there are a lot of ways to taunt people, 
including, "Oh, *that* reference!  *That's* been refuted ages ago!"

The best interpretation I have of Tom's idea is, if someone hasn't made
a good case, don't feel obliged to answer it.

For the most part I don't care who has responsibility to provide
evidence for what.  If it's against the extropian basics, I just don't
want to hear it debated either way.

Who has the burdon of proof in an extropian-basics debate shouldn't be 
of concern to the list because the whole conversation shouldn't be *on*
the list...  But since people have a hard time backing off...

I suggest a prefix, NONEX, for non-extropian, and a rule of ettiquete:
if somebody points out that a thread has gotten into debating extropian
basics, then either take it off the list completely or add NONEX to
the subject line.

