From: pmetzger@shearson.com (Perry E. Metzger)
Subject: Slave Schools

A few people have been commenting that the pernicious influence of the
Government schools is exagerated. I must admit that the Government schools
did their job quite successfully on me for a while -- I was once a confirmed
socialist. Luckily, I escaped, thanks to exposure to some fairly awful human 
beings who happened to be socialists, the Real World (TM) and the influence 
of a few key individuals who deprogrammed me and rescued my mind. Had it not 
been for the overt reverse racism of a group at my university and a very
good economics professor, I might still be a wobbly-brained fool today.

Never underestimate the effect of having skewed evidence and a monolithic
world view pounded into your mind day after day after day as a child. Also
don't underestimate the power of being in an environment in which there is
tremendous pressure to conform to the ideas of your teachers. I will point
out, incidently, that this is just as bad in general in the private schools,
except that they generally teach skills better.

None of this is to say that I would want my children growing up brainwashed
in favor of Extropian memes. However, I would want to expose them equally
to all the evidence and teach them how to reason for themselves, things that
the Government schools do not do.

Perry

